From 65bedd3cc0d9e876fbc5bff11594345ddfdec620 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lucie Defraiteur <luciedefraiteur@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 00:15:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(attention): read the materialized mask with its own row
 stride

The materialized mask reader strides tile rows by seq_kv (it carried a
`TODO not sure if mandatory`). That holds for a contiguous
[batch, heads, seq_q, seq_kv] mask only. A padding mask usually comes as
[batch, 1, 1, seq_kv] broadcast to the full shape, with a stride of 0 on
seq_q: every row after the first was then read from other batches' rows,
or past the end of the buffer.

The reader now takes the tensor's stride(2), which equals seq_kv for a
contiguous mask and 0 for a mask broadcast over seq_q.
